1. Create a main folder using the following naming convention: "company name – RFP title – date of Submission"

   - **a. example:  ABDX, Inc. – AIPrepRFP – 08.08.2025**

2. Included within the main folder should be two subfolders: one for the Administrative Proposal and one for the Technical Proposal.

3. All documents in these folders should be clearly labeled.

4. Upload the main folder to the Dropbox as follows:

   - a. Click the following link: **<u>https://www.dropbox.com/request/AIPrep</u>** <u>.</u>

   - b. Choose the following option: Add Files > Folders from computer.

**Proposals deemed to arrive late will not be considered for award.**

## **VIII. QUESTIONS**

Questions or requests for clarification regarding the RFP should be submitted via email, citing the RFP page and section, in accordance with the schedule in Section V (Schedule of Dates) to <u>AI.Prep@esd.ny.gov . Questions will not be accepted orally, and any question received after the</u> deadline may not be answered. The comprehensive list of questions/requests for clarifications and the official responses will be posted as an Addendum to this RFP.

Respondents are strongly encouraged to review all posted questions and answers, through which ESD may offer clarifications regarding sections of the RFP or advise of material changes thereto.

## **IX. GENERAL PROVISIONS**

The issuance of this RFP and the submission of a response by a Respondent or the acceptance of such a response by ESD does not obligate ESD in any manner.  ESD reserves the right to:

- i. amend, modify or withdraw this RFP;

- ii. revise any requirement of this RFP;

- iii. require supplemental statements or information from any responsible party;

- iv. accept or reject any or all responses hereto;

- v. extend the deadline for submission of responses hereto;

- vi. negotiate potential contract terms with any Respondent;

- vii. communicate with any Respondent to correct and/or clarify responses which do not conform to the instructions contained herein;

- viii. cancel, or reissue in whole or in part, this RFP, if ESD determines in its sole discretion that it is in its best interest to do so; and

### **xi. Schedule A**

Following final selection of a Respondent, ESD will prepare a contract defining all project terms and conditions and the Respondent's responsibilities in conformance with Schedule A.  A sample can be found at: https://esd.ny.gov/sites/default/files/ScheduleA-Services_Materials-3818.pdf Please note that Respondents should not provide the information/documentation required by Schedule A (aside from any information/documentation otherwise required by this solicitation) with the submission of a proposal. However, Respondents should thoroughly review the terms set forth in Schedule A, which are standard for all ESD contracts, and submit any concerns in writing together with the Respondent's Administrative Proposal. Failure to submit concerns in a timely manner shall be deemed a waiver of any objections to the terms contained in Schedule A and successful Respondents will be required to accept the terms therein as part of the executed contract between the parties.

### **xii. Project Sunlight**

This procurement is subject to the Public Integrity Reform Act of 2011. Under the Public Integrity Reform Act of 2011, "appearances" (broadly defined and including any substantive interaction that is meant to have an impact on the decision-making process of a state entity) before a public benefit corporation such as ESD by a person (also broadly defined) for the purposes of procuring a state contract (as contemplated in this RFP) must be reported by ESD to a database maintained by the State Office of General Services that is available to members of the public. If in doubt as to the applicability of Project Sunlight, Respondents and their advisors should consult the Laws of 2011, Ch. 399 for guidance.

### **xiii. Insurance Requirements**

The selected Respondent will be required to provide the following insurance (at a minimum and to the extent applicable):

- Commercial General Liability of $1 million per occurrence and $2 million in the aggregate;

- In the event that you are using a vehicle in business, Commercial Automobile insurance

- with a limit of not less than $1 million;

- Sexual Abuse and Molestation Insurance - $1 million;

- Must show evidence of Worker's Compensation & Employer's Liability insurance at State

- statutory limits;

- Must show evidence of Disability insurance coverage at State statutory limits;

NYS Urban Development Corporation d/b/a Empire State Development (ESD) must be named as additional insured on a primary and non-contributory basis on all of the following policies: Commercial General Liability and Auto Liability.  All policies above should include a waiver of subrogation in favor of ESD.
